# captain_view_witness.rish -- the captain reads a peer's work and never its keys.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ca/captain_view_witness.rish
#
# Seated `20260905` on Keaton's word, after the enclosure's display fault made the whole wall look
# like the problem. It was two missing JSON fields, and the wall is worth keeping: `agent-jail.sh`
# binds ONE tree because a shared checkout bit four times in one day (REDS %291).
#
# So the captain's view loosens nothing. Every peer arrives read-only, and the three paths that hold
# credentials rather than work -- `.gnupg-rye`, `.ssh`, `loops/` -- are DENIED outright. The captain
# can read what a peer has not committed, which is the one thing the anointed remote cannot show,
# and cannot become a second writer in it or reach its keys.

say "captain-view: Language EN -- read a peer's work, never a peer's keys."
say "captain-view: Style Gauge, Meter -- every leg entered a real enclosure and tried the thing."
say "captain-view: Lens TAME -- safety first: a flag is an intention, and the kernel is the answer."

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the launcher and its control both live.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the launcher must stand before any reading of its behavior is believed.
let present = run ["test" "-f" "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh"]
assert present.ok else "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh is missing -- there is no enclosure to read"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/captain_view_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "captain-view: a leg read wrong -- see the control's own lines"
assert control.out contains "fail=0" else "captain-view: the control closed with a failing leg"

# invariant: the view stays opt-in. An unattended lap never sets the variable, so the fleet's
# ordinary shape is one tree per ship whatever this witness proves about the captain's.
let optin = run ["grep" "-q" "FLEET_CAPTAIN_VIEW:-0" "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh"]
assert optin.ok else "captain-view: the view is no longer opt-in -- a peer tree would mount on every launch"

say "captain-view: GREEN -- peer work readable, peer tree unwritable, peer keys denied on metal."
